#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""bale — Claude session orchestrator.

The CLI for the Claude tarball workflow: `bale pack` builds request
tarballs, `bale apply` validates and integrates the response tarballs a
worker Claude returns, and the ancillary commands (revert, rollback,
retry, unlock, handoff, config init, status) manage the session
lifecycle around them. BALE.md at the repo root is the canonical design
document — comments below cite its sections. Stdlib-only, Python 3.10+
(3.11+ uses stdlib `tomllib`; 3.10 the vendored parser in
`bin/_bale_toml.py`). The version narrative that once lived here is git
history now — recover any prior revision with a checkout.

Sections:
   1. Imports + constants                                 (~line   145)
   2. Logging                                             (~line   233)
   3. Shell / git helpers                                 (~line   320)
   4. Hashing                                             (~line   359)
   5. Session IDs and the per-day counter                 (~line   375)
   6. Session registry + locks                            (~line   433)
   7. .gitignore handling for the .bale/ directory        (~line   861)
   8. Path-safety checks                                  (~line   891)
   9. Editor invocation                                   (~line   939)
  10. Pack: file enumeration and filtering                (~line  1000)
  11. Pack: scope projection + threshold caps (BALE.md section 7.4) (~line 1377)
  12. Pack: slug validation                               (~line  1660)
  13. Pack: manifest and tarball construction             (~line  1673)
  14. Pack: wizard                                        (~line  1886)
  15. Pack                                                (~line  2176)
  16. Apply: helpers                                      (~line  2952)
  17. Apply: pipeline                                     (~line  3708)
  18. Apply                                               (~line  4581)
  19. Revert                                              (~line  4821)
  20. Retry                                               (~line  5073)
  21. Unlock                                              (~line  5234)
  22. Handoff                                             (~line  5419)
  23. Hook invocation                                     (~line  5871)
  24. Help and completion                                 (~line  6030)
  25. Status                                              (~line  6433)
  26. CLI                                                 (~line  7046)
"""

